WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.200
I'll tell you everything before I end this.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.850
About the truth Makihara won't tell you.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.200
Once Makihara and I were 
Hand Shakers who fought together.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.990
There's no point running!

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.370
Huh? Did I miss?

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:25.880
Oh, no!

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.110
You never watch your feet.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.940
You watch my feet, so it's okay.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.480
Thinking positively, mentally, 
you're extremely near-sighted.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.960
No, no, Nagaoka.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.000
Don't get mad!

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.000
Thinking positively, it turned out all right!

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.550
Shut up! You always...

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.390
You got quiet again!

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.400
Listen, don't try to say anything clever.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.510
You're terrible at it.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.860
Shall I say what you're thinking?

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.390
It was foolish of me to let 
them get so close, right?

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.080
It was a calculated move.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:55.150
Another second and I would've 
defeated the one who was far away.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.150
I knew the other one was closer,

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.290
but you'd handle them.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.530
And if I'm wide open, it makes 
the enemy lower their guard, too.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.560
I've got plenty of data on 
the type of man you are.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.170
Fine.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.670
I'll buy you shumai.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.920
Or do you like ice candy more?

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.170
Three milks.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.930
Don't think I'm that cheap.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:24.930
No, maybe I'll just buy 
as many as you can eat.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.430
You guys fighting again?

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.010
Akutagawa-sensei.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.100
Sensei!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.940
Sorry we couldn't back you up.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.460
No...

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.180
Oh, jeez...

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.450
You fell silent again!

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.580
There's no point in getting 
quiet around Sensei, is there?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.450
It was someone we could deal with easily.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.770
If there's something that bothers me...

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.520
It's that I have to hold hands 
with Mr. Dumbstruck here.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.880
You think I want to either?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.220
God, I hope not!

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.490
I do not!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.470
I know.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.850
Could you not draw attention to it?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.220
It kind of annoys me.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:13.320
Don't just mumble at me!

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.230
Anyway, it's rare for them to come after us.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:21.240
Once the four of us started working 
together, they mostly stopped trying.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:22.670
They were pros.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.480
They probably thought they could do it.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.330
It happens.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:30.240
But our job isn't to fight 
these stupid battles.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.760
It's the experiment, right?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.200
It's to gather data, right?

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.000
Put those two together and 
you've got our research.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.200
If the two of you together make one whole,

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.800
then you're good partners, right?

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.990
It really looks like brain waves, 
or emotions if you prefer,

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.020
have a great effect on the Nimrods.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.520
<b>Akutagawa Lab</b>

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.220
We still don't have quite enough...

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:57.520
No, even thinking positively,
we don't have nearly enough data.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.250
If only Bunbun was here...

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.910
Don't talk about people who aren't here.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.700
I still think the stories

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.450
of mysterious disappearances 
from societies all over the world,

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.920
especially stories of reaching 
other worlds like Arcadia,

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.870
or stories like Kan'u's dream, 
where there are worlds similar to our own...

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.740
The stories of people coming 
back after visiting other worlds

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:23.860
are evidence that Hand Shakers
 existed in the past.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.430
Stories, huh?

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.800
What about that paper written by 
the Middle Eastern researcher?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.060
Sure, I'll take care of it.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.060
Leave it to me!

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.810
Talented students... no, subordinates.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.260
The fact that there are two pairs
 of Hand Shakers, including us,

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.820
gives us an environment where 
we can actually collect data.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.820
This is ideal, isn't it?

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:52.060
Sensei's partner is his cute bride, though.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.630
But mine is...

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.830
That's what I want to say.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.020
You're laughing too much.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.340
Hey, are you okay?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.230
Lately I've been feeling sick sometimes...

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:08.090
Sit down.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:31.870
Sensei!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.210
Akutagawa-sensei!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.070
Congratulations on the birth.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.260
Here's a present.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.870
Nagaoka didn't bring anything, though.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:43.130
You...

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.260
Thanks.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.310
No, more importantly,

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.130
sorry for getting you hurt like that.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.790
Me, too...

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.280
If I wasn't in this state...

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.730
It's fine.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:59.890
The result was something incredible, right?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.990
This fact overturns all our theories...

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.320
Makihara!

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:10.760
No, that's not the only 
thing I'm celebrating...

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.270
That's just what researchers are like.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:17.000
But I'm really grateful to you.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.760
I didn't think we'd be pulled into 
the Ziggurat during the birth.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:25.170
The two of them were able to 
be born because you were here.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.670
Mayumi and Koyori were born...

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.480
Children born in the Ziggurat?

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.930
<b>Akutagawa Lab</b>

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.940
Let's do it.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.420
Sorry! Sorry!

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.190
Look!

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.620
We're inside the Ziggurat...

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:27.110
If the two of them are here, it means 
that even without thinking positively...

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:28.300
Yes.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.470
My children are born Hand Shakers.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:38.540
They were born with the ability to wield 
the power of God by holding hands.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.070
They are blessed children.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:45.620
Our daughters have shown us 
the form of a new humanity.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:52.260
Or... perhaps you could say this is 
what humans are really meant to be?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.540
It's always...

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.190
So mean...

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:16.950
This is...

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.090
There's something I have to do.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:25.160
I'll do what it takes to make that happen.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.960
I have to pick opponents
that I can actually beat.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.460
I'm sorry.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:32.460
Children are an easy target.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.470
Are you okay?

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.230
How many times has this happened?

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:53.230
I want to believe in the good of humanity...

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.430
Blessings... A new humanity...

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:04.470
What we're truly supposed to be?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.650
Everyone's after them and,
unlike the rest of us, they'll die if they lose.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.500
If they let go of each other's 
hands, they'll disappear!

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.440
I...

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.010
I was wrong.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.900
This is a curse!

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:35.460
No... I don't want to live anymore!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.000
I don't want to live anymore!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.130
I brought shumai.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:56.250
But you're not in the mood, are you?

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.270
Welcome back, Sensei, ma'am.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:12.440
I'm sorry. The two of them were attacked...

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.170
Even though I was there, too...

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.200
You defeated the enemy, right?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.780
That's all that matters.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:20.030
No matter who they are.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.430
Honestly, I would've liked 
to finish them myself.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.770
We took care of ours, too.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.450
They were fools.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:31.580
They gave their real names, so we took 
them out before they entered the Ziggurat.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.290
Again?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.130
Just a little more...

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.200
Just a little more!

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.790
Our Nimrods are starting 
to overwrite the Ziggurat.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.810
One of the ones we crushed before said

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.750
that when the Nimrods overwrite the Ziggurat

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.400
the Hand Shakers will reach God.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:12:00.070
B-But that's... We don't have the data yet...

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.790
It's hypothetically possible 
 he was just imagining it.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.820
We put theory into practice, Makihara.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:10.700
Sometimes it's better to actually put things 
into practice than wait for detailed data.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:13.000
Now is that time.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.210
Shut up!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.710
Sensei...

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.810
I won't let anyone take you.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:25.640
If it was God who put this curse on you,

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.710
if you're trapped by the 
fate of being Hand Shakers,

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.230
we have to release you.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.330
Because I'm your father.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.460
Even if it costs me my life...

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:39.920
I can tell. I can tell!

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.500
Just one more...

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.560
If I defeat one more pair and 
steal everything they have,

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.740
we will gain the right to reach God!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.520
Finally!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.080
Just wait, Mayumi, Koyori!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.750
I promise. I promise!

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:02.810
Just like he said he would, 
Sensei beat the last pair of Hand Shakers.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.240
And then he disappeared.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.420
Did he find God?

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:09.110
Did he challenge Him?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.670
Did he just die?

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.020
We didn't know then,

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:17.020
and I still don't know now.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:27.160
Why isn't CEO Okuike here?

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.540
He was the sponsor, right?

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.950
It's strange, huh?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.770
Empty coffins.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.580
We didn't know for sure that they were dead.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:36.330
It's been a month.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.750
Mayumi-chan! Koyori-chan!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.650
Mayumi! Koyori! Hey!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.360
We kept them alive.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.760
But they're in a coma, huh?

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.860
Perhaps that's why it kept that other 
characteristic of theirs in check.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:12.010
They've lost their parents, their memories,

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.330
their emotions, and now their bodies?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.870
What did these kids do?

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.580
Why is this happening to them?

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.940
What happened?

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.490
It just came out of nowhere...

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.900
Did Akutagawa-sensei do something?

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.320
Was his wish...

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:30.390
Even partial loss of organ function isn't 
normally something you could survive.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:35.390
It was a true miracle that someone was able 
to donate their organs, and the twins lived.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.070
For now, let's think positive, and...

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.400
Can you do that?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.260
I...

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.410
This isn't what Sensei would want.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.930
That isn't God.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:56.090
No, I don't care if it's God.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.660
What are you doing?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.920
What am I doing?

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.280
I'm carrying on Sensei's will.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:13.180
What?

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.450
Sensei fought for them.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.370
He didn't come back,

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.690
but this was the result.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:23.440
So I will kill God.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.340
What are you talking about?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.440
You know what happened to Sensei, right?

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:33.950
What we need to do now is work together 
and figure out what happened to them,

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.950
and find a way for the twins to survive.

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.710
That won't save them.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.960
Stop it!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.910
You saw his face, right?

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.960
Was that the Sensei we knew?

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.210
And what was the result?

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.720
If we're going to save them, 
we need to do it together, right?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.720
As researchers... As Hand Shakers!

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.230
When will that research end?

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.230
What do you mean?

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.230
This is the end for you and me.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:11.460
What's wrong? What was that sound?

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:22.070
And so Koyori-kun lost her partner,

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.250
her older sister Mayumi.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.450
I kept her alive by putting her to sleep.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.260
You just ran away by keeping things 
in the same state they were in.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.610
Maybe.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:40.560
If nothing else, that's how it was back then.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:44.770
But what did you do to Mayumi-kun?

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.370
I used a method to keep her alive.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:49.770
It was your idea.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.280
That's right, but...

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.550
Implanted suggestions using drugs?

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:55.780
That will destroy her heart!

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:57.840
I refuse to accept it.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.210
Drugs?

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.790
I had a theory,

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.480
but I'm sure of it now.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:08.790
Two people connected to each other 
in some form become Hand Shakers.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.780
It can be a shared goal, or love.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:15.800
Connected emotions create this power.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:20.880
That's how Nagaoka and I 
stopped being Hand Shakers.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.560
Because the connection between us broke.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:27.440
Emotions are electromagnetic 
signals created by the brain.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.440
Or perhaps psychological hallucinations 
are emotions, as well.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:33.440
Mayumi loves me.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:37.950
You once refused to use that method!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.950
Our past doesn't matter.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.950
Sis...

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.730
Awaza Kodama...

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.960
I am on a higher plane than her.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.340
A few more pairs

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.010
and I will reach God,

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.970
the same place Sensei did.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.250
How do you know Kodama-san's name?

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:04.120
We were using each other.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:07.830
I was the one who sent her after you.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.730
You told her where we were?

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.330
Indeed.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:17.200
Even if you run now, I know you.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.740
I'll do whatever it takes.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:23.490
Don't you understand what 
happened to Sensei then?

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.360
We are strong.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.840
I understand your power, as well.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.500
I saw your battle with the Houjou siblings.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:31.750
I see.

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:34.750
The reason we couldn't 
immediately leave the Ziggurat,

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:37.760
and that Kodama-san knew my Ziggurat...

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.720
There was still a Hand Shaker 
in the area who was our enemy.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.070
That's why we couldn't leave.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:44.400
Was that you?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:49.160
Houjou Lily, Houjou Masaru. 
Awaza Kodama. Moriyama Hibiki.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.770
I saw your battles with all of them.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:55.850
I know all about the power of 
Single Gear and Sprocket Gear.

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:57.780
You can't beat me.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:01.070
You used Kodama-san and President Lily?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.780
Will you lose the battle, 
and lose Koyori-chan?

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:05.540
Tazuna-kun.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:06.920
I have a proposal.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.080
Put Koyori to sleep again.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.730
I'll take care of the rest.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.040
I will take on this challenge.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:23.790
I think what you're doing is probably right.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:26.560
But I don't want to be separated from Koyori.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.060
We decided together.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.060
Yes, together.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.060
That isn't your little sister.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:33.810
Yes, I know.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.070
If we fight, I will destroy her.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.260
I won't let you.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:39.240
I won't let her sleep alone again.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.820
The way you do things doesn't mesh.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.550
Nagaoka, just like you said,

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:48.600
putting Koyori to sleep was 
just delaying the problem.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.580
Running away by maintaining the status quo.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.830
There's no way for me to deny that.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.080
But you saw it, right?

00:19:56.260 --> 00:20:00.480
How Koyori-kun, who'd lost her memories 
and emotions, began to change...

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.440
By using a different method than you,

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:04.270
she's becoming who she should be.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:07.100
She's communicating heart to heart,

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:10.100
even with the people she 
fought as Hand Shakers!

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:14.100
Nagaoka, are you okay with this?

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.860
Your resolve is strong?

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.260
I'm not scared if I'm with Koyori.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.650
I believe in her.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.980
Because we're together.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.450
Because we're connected.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:24.460
It's okay.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.370
That is what it means for 
us to be Hand Shakers!

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:30.710
I see.

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:31.370
Mayumi...

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.150
Tazuna-kun!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:39.870
Thinking positively...

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.130
No, I don't need to do that, do I?

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.500
You guys can win.

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:00.980
Tazuna, look.

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:14.500
It's not your Ziggurat...

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.500
This is his Nimrod.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:21.050
Gold Cocoon

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.010
and Silver Cocoon.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.890
Let's begin.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:37.200
You who would meet and challenge God...

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:40.020
You, the Hand Shakers...

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:13.120
<i>Heavy and quiet like the rain.</i>

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:15.120
<i>Violent and strong like the wind.</i>

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>The storm slams against the fortress</i>

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:19.960
<i>and reflects what's in both of their hearts.</i>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.290
<i>Souls that seek to protect 
clash again and again,</i>

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:25.480
<i>and the thunder clouds are 
lit up by flashes of light.</i>

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:28.360
<i>You who received the Revelation of Babel.</i>

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:29.170
<i>You are...</i>

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:34.740
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers, 
Episode 12: Shake the Hands.</i>

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:38.660
<i>The gears of fate will spin forever.</i>
